 "summary": "A platinum resistance temperature detector built as a 1206 surface-mount chip, specified to DIN EN 60751. It comes as Pt100 or Pt1000 (100 Ω or 1000 Ω at 0 °C), each in tolerance class F 0.3 (B) or F 0.6 (2B), with a temperature coefficient of 3850 ppm/K. Both classes hold from -50 °C to +130 °C; on circuit board materials whose expansion matches the chip it can be used up to +150 °C. The ends are tin over a nickel barrier, for reflow or wave soldering, and the parts ship face up on blister reels of 4000. It is RoHS compliant.",
